# Resume Writing

- Keep public resume drafts ATS-friendly, concise, and outcome-focused.
- Prefer bullet structure like `scope + action + result` over generic traits or vague claims.
- Order dated resume entries reverse-chronologically, with the newest items first at the top of each section.
- If an employer block is split into dated project or subrole blocks, omit the parent date line and keep dates only on the sub-blocks.
- Use present tense only for role or project blocks whose end date is `present`; use past tense for every block with a closed end date, even when it is nested under a currently active employer.
- Format dated role headings as `Title, Project` when a project or subrole name exists.
- In Russian resume drafts, prefer `Русский title (English title)` for role names when it improves searchability; use the standard spelling `Team Lead`, not `Teamlead`.
- In Russian resume drafts, keep headings, placeholders, and narrative text in Russian; allow English for brands, technology names, search-oriented role aliases in parentheses, and established project or product names when that wording is clearer than a forced translation.
- Keep recent leadership roles detailed and compress older supporting roles when space is tight.
- Keep facts separate from positioning: factual updates belong in `cv.master.yaml`, while summary and emphasis belong in draft resumes.
- When material experience updates change current scope, leadership level, or impact, review and refresh `Summary` / `Профиль` and `Selected Impact` / `Ключевые результаты` in both resume drafts.
- Do not invent titles, dates, metrics, team sizes, stack details, or achievements. Use placeholders until the user confirms them.
- Keep English resume content in English and Russian resume content in Russian. User-facing chat stays in Russian.

Examples:
- Good: `Led a 7-person cross-functional team and aligned a one-year turnaround plan with business stakeholders.`
- Bad: `Hard-working`, `Proud Geek`, psychometric labels, or decorative fluff in public resume drafts.
